		//story
		"sam.event.natural.21": "A ghost story, huh? Hmmm... well, there's one Seb told me once, I'll see if I can remember it all...",
		"sam.event.natural.22.first": "We snuggle up by the fire, soaking in the warmth as Sam launches into his tale.",
		"sam.event.natural.22.third": "They snuggle up by the fire, soaking in the warmth as Sam launches into his tale.",
		"sam.event.natural.23": "Once an adventurer and his favorite tracking hound set out to follow some rumored monster trails in the woods. He was very skilled, and often hunted alone.#$b#After a few days, the dog returned to town, but the adventurer didn't, so his wife commissioned a team of guild members to find her husband.#$b#They took the dog with them hoping he would show them the way to his master.#$b#When they reached the woods, the dog let out a long howl and raced into the trees, only pausing to allow the searchers to catch up.#$b#At one point, they lost sight of the hound just as one of their team stumbled upon two bodies, the lost adventurer and his dog that had been leading them.",
		"sam.event.natural.24": "They were confused, but they didn't want to leave the lost man's wife to worry so they retrieved the dog's collar and the hunter's belongings.#$b#Planning to send another team back to the site to investigate, they hurried back to the adventurer's farmhouse where they handed the collar and belongings to his distraught wife.#$b#'Look!' a member of the team hissed, pointing a shaking finger towards the fireplace.#$b#There, curled up in the fire's glow, was the faithful dog. The hound raised his head, gave a lazy shake of his ears, and faded away.",
		"sam.event.natural.25": "Later, after investigating the site in the woods, it was reported that the adventurer and his dog had fallen to a very large bear.#$b#The hound had fought to the last trying to protect his master, and his spirit had refused to rest until his mistress knew what had become of them.#$b#Oddly though, there had never been a report of a bear attack in those woods before and any bears spotted had been shy and reclusive.",
		"sam.event.natural.26": "Months later, the adventurer's wife woke in the dead of night... SCRAPE... SCRAPE... claws drug down the wall right outside her room.#$b#Terrified, she ran to the kitchen where she kept a rifle by the door. SNUFF SNUFF GRRRRRR... scratching and clawing... it was the bear!#$b#Silence for a moment, then SCREEEECH... a claw scraping down the window pane... then BLAM!! A shotgun! A dog's barking and a man's shout drove the bear back into the woods.#$b#With a trembling hand, the woman pulled back the curtain to peek out... and striding away across the field, she saw her husband and faithful hound dog.#$b#They seemed to flicker in the moonlight when she heard her husband's familiar chuckle as he turned to smile and wave to her in farewell before fading away.",
		"sam.event.natural.27": "The next morning, she looked around her house, but found no marks of claws or footprints anywhere. There was no sign of the bear.#$b#To this day, no one knows what manner of creature was stalking the adventurer and his family, or why.",
		"sam.event.natural.28.first": "Sam sits silently for moment, then shivers... I grin and wrap my arms around him.",
